<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>Structured address elements</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Elements</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">Structured address elements</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block">The <strong>structured address elements</strong> are the dedicated ISO 20022 XML fields that replace free-text address lines: <code>&lt;StrtNm&gt;</code> (street, 70 chars), <code>&lt;BldgNb&gt;</code> (16), <code>&lt;BldgNm&gt;</code> (35), <code>&lt;PstCd&gt;</code> (16), <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> (35), <code>&lt;CtrySubDvsn&gt;</code> (ISO 3166-2) and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code>. <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> are mandatory; <code>&lt;PstCd&gt;</code> is Required-Conditional under the CPMI model.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How Structured address elements works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>All structured elements are optional-but-recommended except the mandatory pair; in fully structured format <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> is excluded altogether. <code>&lt;CtrySubDvsn&gt;</code>, where used, must carry an ISO 3166-2 code such as <code>US-CA</code> or <code>GB-ENG</code>. Text fields must contain at least one character, with no leading or trailing whitespace.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §3.2–§3.3 (Table 5); CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.13–§0.31 / p5; §4 footnote / p6-4.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>All premises and location elements in use:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;StrtNm&gt;</span>CUBA STREET<span class="tag">&lt;/StrtNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;BldgNb&gt;</span>169<span class="tag">&lt;/BldgNb&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;PstCd&gt;</span>6011<span class="tag">&lt;/PstCd&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>WELLINGTON<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
